# text = Observing my hesitation , and no doubt attributing it , naturally enough , to some momentary shyness on my part , Miss Halcombe took the business of talking , as easily and readily as usual , into her own hands she said , pointing to the sketch-book on the table , and to the little delicate wandering hand that was still trifling with it Miss Fairlie laughed with a ready good-humour , which broke out as brightly as if it had been part of the sunshine above us , over her lovely face she said , her clear , truthful blue eyes looking alternately at Miss Halcombe and at me She made the confession very prettily and simply , and , with quaint , childish earnestness , drew the sketch-book away close to her own side of the table .
