# text = Considering the relative ages of the two ladies , the aunt's chance , in the ordinary course of nature , of receiving the ten thousand pounds , was thus rendered doubtful in the extreme ; and Madame Fosco resented her brother's treatment of her as unjustly as usual in such cases , by refusing to see her niece , and declining to believe that Miss Fairlie's intercession had ever been exerted to restore her name to Mr . Fairlie's will .
