# text = The unfortunate woman's last idea in connection with Sir Percival was the idea of annoying and distressing him , and of elevating herself , as she supposed , in the estimation of the patients and nurses , by assuming the character of his deceased wife , the scheme of this personation having evidently occurred to her after a stolen interview which she had succeeded in obtaining with Lady Glyde , and at which she had observed the extraordinary accidental likeness between the deceased lady and herself .
