# text = I sat down in the vacant chair -- gently unclasped the poor , worn , restless fingers , and took both her hands in mine She struggled with herself , and raised her eyes to mine she said She stopped , bent forward a little , and laid her head on my shoulder , with a terrible mute helplessness that struck me to the heart I repeated gently she answered , with a weary , hopeless sigh I raised her head , and smoothed away the tangled hair that fell over her face , and kissed her -- my poor , faded flower ! my lost , afflicted sister I said She looked at me with a feverish eagerness , with a breathless interest , that made me tremble for the new life of hope which I had called into being by those few words .
