# text = She could not call the colour that had left it back to her face , but she had steadied her voice , she had recovered the defiant self-possession of her manner when she answered me she said I walked to the door , waited a moment before I opened it , and turned round to look at her again I said She stopped , her pale face darkened , and she stole back with a quiet , stealthy , cat-like step to her chair she said , sitting down again , with the mockery of a smile just hovering on her cruel lips , and the furtive light of hatred lurking deep in her steady eyes .
