# text = The extraordinary anxiety which he had expressed to remain unenlightened as to the Count's identity -- or , in other words , to be left uncertain enough about facts to justify him to his own conscience in remaining passive -- betrayed plainly that the means of exercising the terrible justice of the Brotherhood were ready to his hand , although , as a naturally humane man , he had shrunk from plainly saying as much in my presence .
